    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under the CIF (Cost, Insurance, and Freight) Incoterm 2020, the seller is responsible for arranging and paying for the carriage of the goods to the destination port. However, the seller must also provide insurance coverage for the shipment, usually against the perils of sea carriage. The risk of loss or damage to the goods passes to the buyer as soon as the goods have been delivered to the carrier. The buyer assumes subsequent costs, risks, and transportation once the goods have arrived at the port of destination.",
